      "content": "Some commentators argue that prioritizing emotional validation over immediate behavioral correction can inadvertently teach children that negative or disruptive behavior is acceptable. Another point raised is that without consistent, firm limits, children may struggle to navigate societal expectations regarding rules and obedience. Critics also suggest that an overemphasis on avoiding conflict can prevent children from developing crucial conflict-resolution skills in high-stakes situations. Furthermore, some assert that a constant focus on internal emotional states might overshadow the need for external behavioral accountability. Finally, some viewpoints hold that excessive permissiveness can inhibit the development of grit and perseverance when faced with genuine adversity.",
